photographs and videos show the  devastating toll of harvey on texans one  of the most memorable images though is  from a nursing home we all remember this  picture of the resident sitting in  waist-deep water it spread very quickly  online and not long after another  picture showed the residents safe and  dry at another facility jamie yuka spoke  to one of the women in the original  picture she's in dickinson southeast of  houston jamie good morning  good morning the name of the small  nursing home is la vita bella which  means the beautiful life in italian but  life became unbearable for the residents  here when flood waters came rushing into  the home during hurricane harvey we  spoke with former resident ruth miller  she recounted what happened  can you tell me about being in the water  i like it you didn't like it  it's scary  yeah  i love your safe as the water rose  around ruth miller and her friends the  64 year old says staffers at lavita  bella relied on a simple mantra  keep calm and collected  do they just keep saying that over and  over again  keep calm and collected so that's fine  oh smells good doesn't it nursing  homeowners trudy and pete lamson say  they were initially told to shelter in  place that is where the water rose in  this room but evacuation was soon their  only option within about 45 minutes to  an hour it went from ankle  to stomach to get help trudy snapped  this photo of residents in rising water  and sent it to her daughter in florida  i told my daughter do what you have to  do a few hours after the image was  posted on social media came the rescues  then the reunions  what was it like when you first saw me  today oh  it was  happy ruth is now living with her older  sister susan baubrick when you look at  that picture again what goes through  your mind how tragic this could have  ended up  i think the water level rose there and  it and luckily it held  it held  ruth will stay with her sister until the  family can find a new facility to fit  her needs as for the owners of the  nursing home they plan to rebuild but  you can see there's plenty of damage  outside as well as inside so there's no  telling when residents would be able to  return here maurice okay jamie thank you  you could feel their gratitude but let's  let's hear for social media all right a  few hours that's right and these folks  were rescued in a way that wasn't  probably possible or likely years ago  and we got to see that story from  beginning to end and there was a happy  ending there very very
 

